{"id":"tia","lemma":"tia","pos":"noun","rank":698,"glosses":["aunt (sister of someone's father or mother, or an uncle's wife)","aunt (colloquial term of address for an older woman)","colloquial term of address for any female person"],"ipa":"/ˈt͡ʃi.ɐ/","audio":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/transcoded/3/31/LL-Q5146_%28por%29-Santamarcanda-tia.wav/LL-Q5146_%28por%29-Santamarcanda-tia.wav.mp3","gender":"f","forms":{"plural":"tias","masculine":"tio","masculinePlural":"tios"},"formAudio":{"tio":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/3/3b/LL-Q5146_%28por%29-Nelson_Ricardo_2500-tio.wav"},"examples":[{"text":"Minha tia tem três filhos.","en":"My aunt has three children.","audio":"https://tatoeba.org/en/audio/download/49954","words":[{"g":"my, mine","l":"meu"},null,{"g":"has / there is","l":"ter"},{"g":"three"},{"g":"children (one's direct…"}]},{"text":"Minha tia parece jovem.","en":"My aunt looks young.","words":[{"g":"my, mine","l":"meu"},null,{"g":"to seem","l":"parecer"},{"g":"young, youthful"}]},{"text":"Minha tia me trouxe flores.","en":"My aunt brought me flowers.","words":[{"g":"my, mine","l":"meu"},null,{"g":"me"},{"g":"bring","l":"trazer"},{"g":"flower","l":"flor"}]},{"text":"Minha tia teve uma vida feliz.","en":"My aunt lived a happy life.","words":[{"g":"my, mine","l":"meu"},null,{"g":"to own","l":"ter"},{"g":"a","l":"um"},{"g":"state of being alive"},{"g":"happy"}]},{"text":"Ela parece com a sua tia.","en":"She resembles her aunt.","words":[{"g":"she"},{"g":"to seem","l":"parecer"},{"g":"with"},{"g":"the / to"},{"g":"his","l":"seu"},null]}]}